1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,643
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:06,643 --> 00:00:10,616
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,616 --> 00:00:13,008
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:13,008 --> 00:00:13,795
Boxing Club.

5
00:00:13,795 --> 00:00:15,513
I think the one who bullied him is someone close to him.

6
00:00:15,513 --> 00:00:16,650
Please let me go with you.

7
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:17,520
I’m worried about you.

8
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:18,445
Why are you worried about me?

9
00:00:18,445 --> 00:00:20,424
If I don’t worry about you, who am I supposed to worry about?

10
00:00:20,569 --> 00:00:21,863
I like you.

11
00:00:21,863 --> 00:00:22,834
Oh.

12
00:00:22,834 --> 00:00:24,153
You cheeky kid.

13
00:00:24,153 --> 00:00:24,841
Where’s P’Niran?

14
00:00:24,841 --> 00:00:26,474
He got out of the car and stormed off somewhere.

15
00:00:26,474 --> 00:00:27,552
P’Niran!

16
00:00:27,552 --> 00:00:28,936
Do you understand me, Cheewa?

17
00:00:28,936 --> 00:00:30,296
Everyone I love

18
00:00:30,379 --> 00:00:31,639
might all be gone.

19
00:00:31,639 --> 00:00:33,008
I’ll be right here for you.

20
00:01:37,525 --> 00:01:40,093
You’ve been crying for hours already,
P’Niran.

21
00:01:40,714 --> 00:01:46,107
Did you know that crying for hours
can wear your body out?

22
00:01:46,293 --> 00:01:48,173
It’s no different from playing sports.

23
00:01:52,664 --> 00:01:54,441
Can you not talk about sports?

24
00:01:58,796 --> 00:01:59,408
Oh…

25
00:02:01,291 --> 00:02:02,253
I’m sorry.

26
00:02:02,253 --> 00:02:03,807
I didn’t mean to.

27
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,249
How about we do something fun?

28
00:02:15,032 --> 00:02:16,170
Let me catch you.

29
00:02:16,356 --> 00:02:17,757
Let me catch you.

30
00:02:19,268 --> 00:02:20,204
Hey!

31
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:21,612
Aha!

32
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:24,150
No, I didn’t catch it.

33
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:25,304
Why is it so hard to catch?

34
00:02:27,022 --> 00:02:28,409
Let me catch you, alien.

35
00:02:28,409 --> 00:02:29,364
I’m sad, you know?

36
00:02:29,364 --> 00:02:30,879
Let me catch you. I’m sad.

37
00:02:30,879 --> 00:02:31,627
Being sad has nothing to do with it.

38
00:02:31,627 --> 00:02:32,569
Don’t use that as an excuse.

39
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,304
You have to use your own skills.

40
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:47,234
You made this really well.

41
00:02:47,399 --> 00:02:48,344
Aren’t you going to eat?

42
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:51,498
I don’t like it. It’s spicy.

43
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:57,451
Such a baby.

44
00:02:59,189 --> 00:03:00,160
Yes, I am.

45
00:03:02,312 --> 00:03:04,268
No one’s good at everything.

46
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:06,910
But…

47
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,099
You’re the best in my eyes, P’Niran.

48
00:03:10,699 --> 00:03:13,820
Even if there are more things
you feel like you’re not good at, that’s okay.

49
00:03:15,413 --> 00:03:18,553
I’ll cheer you on for eternity.

50
00:03:21,499 --> 00:03:22,149
Mm.

51
00:03:34,918 --> 00:03:35,773
Are you sure you don’t want to eat this?

52
00:03:36,146 --> 00:03:36,810
I can feed you.

53
00:03:36,955 --> 00:03:38,920
Want a bite if I feed you?

54
00:03:40,555 --> 00:03:42,851
No, thank you. It’s not worth it.

55
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,322
If I toss and turn in my sleep, wake me up.

56
00:03:48,681 --> 00:03:49,840
You won’t.

57
00:03:50,026 --> 00:03:52,239
Your bed is big. Even if you do, it’s fine.

58
00:03:52,239 --> 00:03:52,910
You won’t hit me.

59
00:04:17,155 --> 00:04:17,853
Cheewa.

60
00:04:25,448 --> 00:04:26,154
Thank you.

61
00:04:26,444 --> 00:04:27,731
What are you thanking me for?

62
00:04:33,011 --> 00:04:34,308
I’m thankful we met.

63
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:37,528
Thank you for liking P’Niran.

64
00:04:39,287 --> 00:04:41,160
Thank you for not letting me cry alone.

65
00:04:46,189 --> 00:04:48,368
The stars are more beautiful tonight
than ever.

66
00:04:51,928 --> 00:04:55,634
♪ And I’ll still be here ♪

67
00:04:55,634 --> 00:04:59,805
♪ Every turn, I’ll be near ♪

68
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:01,725
You can get a free hug.

69
00:05:02,718 --> 00:05:03,775
You know that, right?

70
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:06,165
Nice try.

71
00:05:06,165 --> 00:05:09,299
♪ Right here for life ♪

72
00:05:09,299 --> 00:05:12,098
♪ Just like you prayed to the stars ♪

73
00:05:12,098 --> 00:05:13,640
Are we boyfriends yet?

74
00:05:14,737 --> 00:05:15,760
Funny.

75
00:05:19,237 --> 00:05:21,692
I wish I could watch the stars
with someone I love.

76
00:05:23,699 --> 00:05:24,736
Seriously, kid?

77
00:05:24,736 --> 00:05:25,726
You’re down bad.

78
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:36,607
♪ Whenever you need me ♪

79
00:05:36,607 --> 00:05:40,896
♪ Just know I’m keeping you in my sight ♪

80
00:05:45,229 --> 00:05:46,346
Good night.

81
00:05:55,187 --> 00:05:58,442
You know we can
have a good night kiss, right?

82
00:06:02,581 --> 00:06:03,797
Do you want to?

83
00:06:12,458 --> 00:06:14,853
Just answer based on what you want.

84
00:06:15,288 --> 00:06:16,210
For example,

85
00:06:16,541 --> 00:06:19,680
you love singing.

86
00:06:20,094 --> 00:06:22,356
But you’re interested in going to law school.

87
00:06:22,356 --> 00:06:23,700
That’s fine too.

88
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,512
Go ahead and write it down.

89
00:06:25,512 --> 00:06:28,408
After that, leave your paper on my desk.

90
00:06:28,408 --> 00:06:31,207
Then you can go on your lunch break.

91
00:06:37,524 --> 00:06:39,250
SELF-DISCOVERY ASSESSMENT
PIANGNIRAN KITTIMETEE

92
00:06:40,037 --> 00:06:41,085
Are you guys done?

93
00:06:41,085 --> 00:06:42,023
I’m starving.

94
00:06:43,989 --> 00:06:44,684
Let’s go.

95
00:06:55,643 --> 00:06:57,349
What did you write down?

96
00:06:57,928 --> 00:07:00,506
Well… I just wrote down something random.

97
00:07:01,437 --> 00:07:02,761
I bet you wrote judo.

98
00:07:17,754 --> 00:07:18,894
I want to play guitar.

99
00:07:18,894 --> 00:07:19,565
Let’s go get our guitars.

100
00:07:19,565 --> 00:07:20,235
Huh?

101
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:21,076
Sure.

102
00:07:21,076 --> 00:07:21,670
I’ll be right back.

103
00:07:27,341 --> 00:07:30,503
Hey, I think I’m quitting judo.

104
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,142
Why are you quitting?

105
00:07:33,784 --> 00:07:35,250
You seem to enjoy it.

106
00:07:36,119 --> 00:07:37,274
Do you feel pressured?

107
00:07:37,626 --> 00:07:38,709
About making it to the national team?

108
00:07:39,330 --> 00:07:42,835
I started judo because I enjoyed it.

109
00:07:42,835 --> 00:07:47,250
But at some point,
I thought it was time to stop having fun.

110
00:07:47,685 --> 00:07:49,769
I’d rather focus on something else in my life.

111
00:07:52,004 --> 00:07:54,099
Can’t you do both at the same time?

112
00:07:55,796 --> 00:07:58,648
Well, yeah. I can do both.

113
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,807
But deep down I know
I’m not as good at judo as you.

114
00:08:04,918 --> 00:08:06,590
I’ve already given it my all
trying to keep up with you.

115
00:08:08,784 --> 00:08:10,011
Won’t you regret it?

116
00:08:10,011 --> 00:08:11,196
You’ve been practicing for so long.

117
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:13,940
I feel like you even
take it more seriously than I do.

118
00:08:17,313 --> 00:08:18,648
I’ve had fun practicing it.

119
00:08:19,476 --> 00:08:22,676
It’s fine. I don’t regret doing it with you.

120
00:08:39,442 --> 00:08:40,418
Thanks…

121
00:08:41,763 --> 00:08:42,799
for judo.

122
00:08:47,683 --> 00:08:49,179
Because of you,

123
00:08:49,427 --> 00:08:51,074
I got to do something fun for so long.

124
00:09:04,974 --> 00:09:08,484
And you’re free to like
or dislike anything you want.

125
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:11,420
You don’t need to think about anything else.

126
00:09:13,448 --> 00:09:14,685
Just ask yourself what you want.

127
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,035
It’s your life.

128
00:09:19,028 --> 00:09:20,128
You should get to choose.

129
00:09:40,059 --> 00:09:40,984
Hello.

130
00:09:41,232 --> 00:09:42,531
Finally.

131
00:09:42,676 --> 00:09:44,129
I’m just waiting on you.

132
00:09:45,391 --> 00:09:46,736
Have a seat, Niran.

133
00:09:47,551 --> 00:09:48,197
Okay.

134
00:09:54,902 --> 00:09:56,774
“I don’t like doing judo.”

135
00:10:09,098 --> 00:10:09,859
Hi, Coach.

136
00:10:12,301 --> 00:10:13,187
What’s up, Niran?

137
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:14,923
Is everything okay?

138
00:10:16,952 --> 00:10:18,573
Thara has already told you, right?

139
00:10:19,959 --> 00:10:20,803
Yes, he has.

140
00:10:21,548 --> 00:10:23,685
It’s a shame after all the effort he’s put in.

141
00:10:24,554 --> 00:10:25,982
But I get it.

142
00:10:26,499 --> 00:10:29,183
He wants to focus more on his studies.

143
00:10:29,493 --> 00:10:31,962
You guys are going to university soon.

144
00:10:33,887 --> 00:10:37,582
What if I also want to quit judo for good?

145
00:10:42,652 --> 00:10:46,136
I had a huge fight with my dad yesterday.

146
00:10:47,626 --> 00:10:51,527
I told him that judo was his dream.

147
00:10:52,686 --> 00:10:53,728
It’s not mine.

148
00:10:55,218 --> 00:10:57,601
Do you really think that way?

149
00:11:00,519 --> 00:11:03,305
That’s exactly what I’m not sure about.

150
00:11:05,002 --> 00:11:07,102
I don’t know if I really think that way.

151
00:11:09,275 --> 00:11:10,623
I didn’t start judo

152
00:11:11,741 --> 00:11:13,963
because I enjoyed it like other people did.

153
00:11:16,757 --> 00:11:18,669
Sometimes I don’t know what I’m doing.

154
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,752
I just practice because I have to.

155
00:11:30,644 --> 00:11:35,011
Would it be so wrong if I quit judo?

156
00:11:39,999 --> 00:11:41,308
It wouldn’t be wrong at all, Niran.

157
00:11:42,426 --> 00:11:45,015
You have the right
to decide everything for yourself.

158
00:11:45,967 --> 00:11:49,243
I respect all your decisions,

159
00:11:50,278 --> 00:11:52,049
and I’ll keep supporting you.

160
00:11:54,884 --> 00:12:00,683
Then… can I just practice
as much as I feel like today?

161
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:03,487
If I think of anything, I’ll come talk to you.

162
00:12:07,129 --> 00:12:07,950
Of course.

163
00:12:08,364 --> 00:12:11,285
Take all the time you need.

164
00:12:48,408 --> 00:12:49,434
Whoa, P’Niran.

165
00:12:49,537 --> 00:12:50,476
Who made you mad?

166
00:12:50,642 --> 00:12:52,387
You’re really going all out with these throws.

167
00:12:52,573 --> 00:12:53,735
You’re starting to look pale.

168
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:55,001
Give me a second.

169
00:12:58,912 --> 00:12:59,946
Are you okay?

170
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:01,017
Do you want to take a break?

171
00:13:01,265 --> 00:13:02,436
I’m fine.

172
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:06,500
Come on.

173
00:13:17,034 --> 00:13:19,122
P’Niran!

174
00:13:19,122 --> 00:13:19,622
P’Niran!

175
00:13:19,622 --> 00:13:20,438
What’s wrong with P’Niran?

176
00:13:20,438 --> 00:13:21,545
- P’Niran!
- P’Niran!

177
00:13:21,545 --> 00:13:22,591
Can someone go get the teacher, please?

178
00:13:22,591 --> 00:13:24,360
Coach! Something’s wrong with P’Niran!

179
00:13:26,057 --> 00:13:26,715
Niran!

180
00:13:27,687 --> 00:13:28,836
P’Niran, did you know—

181
00:13:28,836 --> 00:13:29,665
“That I’m worried about you”?

182
00:13:30,244 --> 00:13:31,334
P’Niran knows.

183
00:13:31,479 --> 00:13:32,726
He knows Cheewa is worried about him.

184
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:34,272
Give me your hand.

185
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,430
What for?

186
00:13:47,408 --> 00:13:48,447
Everyone, please step back.

187
00:13:48,447 --> 00:13:49,109
Don’t crowd around.

188
00:13:49,931 --> 00:13:50,656
Niran!

189
00:13:51,262 --> 00:13:51,961
Niran!

190
00:13:53,368 --> 00:13:54,013
Niran!

191
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,529
Should we carry him?

192
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,022
Alright, be careful.

193
00:14:00,022 --> 00:14:01,213
Help us.

194
00:14:12,322 --> 00:14:14,888
When I was young,

195
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,721
while my parents were still together,

196
00:14:18,457 --> 00:14:20,455
they fought a lot.

197
00:14:20,845 --> 00:14:23,114
Aren’t you a sports medicine professional?

198
00:14:23,114 --> 00:14:26,732
Isn’t your job to take care of athletes
and get them ready for their matches?

199
00:14:26,732 --> 00:14:28,820
Whenever the higher-ups invite you out
for drinks, you rush right over.

200
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:31,263
Da, it’s not like I want to go.

201
00:14:31,631 --> 00:14:33,756
But they invited us.

202
00:14:33,756 --> 00:14:35,289
Wouldn’t it be rude if we didn’t go?

203
00:14:35,289 --> 00:14:36,105
What is this?

204
00:14:36,105 --> 00:14:37,575
Why are we fighting in front of our son?

205
00:14:37,575 --> 00:14:39,286
Fighting? Who started it?

206
00:14:39,286 --> 00:14:40,014
Huh?

207
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,169
Niran.

208
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:50,413
I didn’t know what their problems were.

209
00:14:51,474 --> 00:14:54,449
I didn’t know what I could do
to get my parents back together.

210
00:14:54,449 --> 00:14:55,016
Hey, son.

211
00:14:55,535 --> 00:14:56,908
What’s up?

212
00:15:04,548 --> 00:15:05,449
Push forward.

213
00:15:05,449 --> 00:15:06,225
Right leg follows.

214
00:15:06,225 --> 00:15:07,469
Yes!

215
00:15:08,118 --> 00:15:09,150
All I knew was…

216
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:09,817
Good.

217
00:15:09,817 --> 00:15:10,613
Come on!

218
00:15:12,063 --> 00:15:14,200
- Our son is confident.
- Everyone seemed to like seeing me do judo.

219
00:15:14,525 --> 00:15:15,347
He trained well.

220
00:15:15,866 --> 00:15:16,552
Begin!

221
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:19,035
Every time I had a judo match,

222
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:23,558
Dad and Mom would come
cheer me on together.

223
00:15:24,322 --> 00:15:25,722
Come on!

224
00:15:26,350 --> 00:15:27,268
Full point!

225
00:15:27,268 --> 00:15:28,145
Awesome!

226
00:15:29,314 --> 00:15:31,558
They seemed to love each other
more than usual.

227
00:15:32,337 --> 00:15:33,696
Well done, son!

228
00:15:34,539 --> 00:15:35,249
Wow.

229
00:15:35,249 --> 00:15:36,885
Come here.

230
00:15:36,885 --> 00:15:38,064
Great job.

231
00:15:38,064 --> 00:15:39,246
You’re amazing.

232
00:15:39,246 --> 00:15:40,363
- Are you tired?
- I told you you could do it.

233
00:15:40,363 --> 00:15:41,059
I’m not tired.

234
00:15:41,059 --> 00:15:42,089
You’re not tired, see?

235
00:15:42,089 --> 00:15:45,062
- I knew you were going to win.
- Piece of cake.

236
00:15:46,924 --> 00:15:49,112
This is what happens when you train hard.

237
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:53,300
Awesome.

238
00:15:53,928 --> 00:15:55,500
Let’s go get some pork BBQ.

239
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,565
Go ahead.

240
00:15:56,717 --> 00:15:59,477
Go wherever and do whatever you want.

241
00:15:59,477 --> 00:16:00,754
Don’t force me!

242
00:16:02,009 --> 00:16:04,371
You’ve been forcing me for 10 years!

243
00:16:05,954 --> 00:16:07,424
I’ve never forced you.

244
00:16:07,424 --> 00:16:11,048
I always explain why we have to do things
and why we have to go.

245
00:16:11,048 --> 00:16:12,808
Why do we have to do it, huh?

246
00:16:12,808 --> 00:16:14,041
Come on, Da.

247
00:16:14,409 --> 00:16:15,167
What?

248
00:16:16,401 --> 00:16:19,016
My ranking went up today.

249
00:16:19,319 --> 00:16:21,018
Wow. Really?

250
00:16:23,096 --> 00:16:24,734
How do you even take care of him?

251
00:16:24,734 --> 00:16:27,025
How could you make him train
until he got hurt like this?

252
00:16:27,198 --> 00:16:29,102
Why do you keep forcing him?

253
00:16:30,452 --> 00:16:32,074
I told you, remember?

254
00:16:32,593 --> 00:16:35,588
I told you not to force your dream on our son.

255
00:16:35,588 --> 00:16:36,660
My dream?

256
00:16:37,461 --> 00:16:39,372
Judo is his dream.

257
00:16:40,043 --> 00:16:41,547
What would you know?

258
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:43,246
You’ve never cared about him.

259
00:16:43,744 --> 00:16:44,476
Listen.

260
00:16:45,039 --> 00:16:47,253
I asked you before.

261
00:16:47,253 --> 00:16:48,651
I asked if I could take him with me.

262
00:16:48,651 --> 00:16:50,036
Remember what you said?

263
00:16:50,036 --> 00:16:52,088
You said you could take
better care of him than I could.

264
00:16:52,088 --> 00:16:53,553
You said you could take care of athletes,

265
00:16:53,553 --> 00:16:54,870
so you could take care of our son.

266
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:56,909
Now why did he end up like this?

267
00:16:56,909 --> 00:16:58,327
How could you let him get hurt like this?

268
00:16:58,327 --> 00:17:01,181
No matter how I raised him,
I never left him to start a new life.

269
00:17:07,587 --> 00:17:08,334
Right?

270
00:17:08,724 --> 00:17:12,564
When you had a chance to start over,
you didn’t hesitate.

271
00:17:13,581 --> 00:17:15,407
Do you know how much that hurt our son?

272
00:17:20,753 --> 00:17:22,207
Well, whose fault was it?

273
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:24,212
Wasn’t it because of you?

274
00:17:24,602 --> 00:17:29,523
You keep forcing everyone in your family
to do everything you want.

275
00:17:30,064 --> 00:17:32,579
Have you ever asked if they wanted to do it?

276
00:17:33,207 --> 00:17:35,869
You only think your opinions matter.

277
00:17:37,384 --> 00:17:41,183
It’s not good for our family,
for me, or for our son.

278
00:17:43,759 --> 00:17:50,145
Have you ever asked him
why he wanted to quit judo?

279
00:17:52,028 --> 00:17:53,495
It’s because of you.

280
00:17:57,607 --> 00:18:00,949
Did you ever really know
why he wanted to do judo in the first place?

281
00:18:03,135 --> 00:18:05,245
Because you forced him to.

282
00:18:08,405 --> 00:18:11,737
I once asked him if he wanted to continue.

283
00:18:11,997 --> 00:18:13,558
If he’d said no,
I wouldn’t have forced him at all.

284
00:18:15,354 --> 00:18:16,504
He said yes.

285
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:19,757
He said he wanted to keep doing judo
because…

286
00:18:26,921 --> 00:18:33,066
Because whenever he did judo,
whenever he had a judo match,

287
00:18:33,997 --> 00:18:36,072
his dad and mom would be there
to cheer him on together.

288
00:18:40,617 --> 00:18:44,330
I know what I said was terrible.

289
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:45,200
It wasn’t pleasant to hear.

290
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,504
It sounded like I was forcing you.

291
00:18:48,106 --> 00:18:50,504
But I wanted you to go watch him.

292
00:18:52,171 --> 00:18:54,033
Our son really needed us.

293
00:18:56,068 --> 00:18:57,205
He thought…

294
00:18:58,525 --> 00:19:03,294
the only time we could be together
as a family

295
00:19:04,917 --> 00:19:06,841
was when he did judo.

296
00:19:14,037 --> 00:19:15,923
I’m not a good father.

297
00:19:16,724 --> 00:19:20,005
But I know that judo

298
00:19:21,975 --> 00:19:24,739
is the only happiness he has left.

299
00:19:27,639 --> 00:19:29,683
The one thing that lets him think of you.

300
00:19:37,179 --> 00:19:39,320
But now he’s grown up enough

301
00:19:40,965 --> 00:19:43,802
to realize that even if
he made the national team,

302
00:19:44,906 --> 00:19:47,575
his family could never be the same.

303
00:20:07,772 --> 00:20:10,260
Oh. Niran.

304
00:20:12,322 --> 00:20:13,135
Hey.

305
00:20:14,022 --> 00:20:14,791
Are you okay?

306
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:22,694
Hey.

307
00:20:40,712 --> 00:20:41,855
Niran.

308
00:20:45,773 --> 00:20:47,344
I’m sorry.

309
00:20:48,322 --> 00:20:49,915
I’m sorry.

310
00:21:15,675 --> 00:21:17,207
I’m sorry, son.

311
00:21:17,207 --> 00:21:18,752
I’m sorry.

312
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,862
I’m sorry.

313
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:24,274
I’m sorry.

314
00:21:39,303 --> 00:21:40,786
I’m sorry, son.

315
00:21:43,708 --> 00:21:45,773
Get plenty of rest.

316
00:21:46,228 --> 00:21:49,144
As for your knee, it's a good thing
we caught it in time.

317
00:21:49,144 --> 00:21:50,503
There weren't any warning signs, right?

318
00:21:51,953 --> 00:21:52,870
No.

319
00:21:54,602 --> 00:21:56,350
Excuse me.

320
00:21:56,393 --> 00:21:56,980
Okay.

321
00:21:57,802 --> 00:21:59,021
- Bye.
- Bye.

322
00:22:03,063 --> 00:22:04,298
It’s okay.

323
00:22:04,861 --> 00:22:06,286
You’ll recover soon.

324
00:22:16,474 --> 00:22:19,009
Nurse, I’ll be fine on my own.

325
00:22:19,009 --> 00:22:19,745
You can go…

326
00:22:24,095 --> 00:22:25,325
Do you believe me now?

327
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:28,388
Believe what?

328
00:22:28,626 --> 00:22:33,109
That crying a lot will wear your body out,
just like exercising.

329
00:22:34,170 --> 00:22:37,634
And you did both, so you got sick.

330
00:22:42,322 --> 00:22:43,427
Why are you smiling?

331
00:22:46,652 --> 00:22:47,678
P’Niran, did you know—

332
00:22:47,678 --> 00:22:48,640
“That I’m worried about you”?

333
00:22:50,826 --> 00:22:51,931
P’Niran knows.

334
00:22:52,234 --> 00:22:53,441
He knows Cheewa is worried about him.

335
00:22:54,647 --> 00:22:55,785
Thank you.

336
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:59,057
P’Niran is so lucky to have you, Cheewa.

337
00:23:07,632 --> 00:23:09,576
What did you say, P’Niran?

338
00:23:13,234 --> 00:23:14,656
You caught me off guard.

339
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:21,680
Give me your hand.

340
00:23:24,471 --> 00:23:26,065
What for?

341
00:23:27,796 --> 00:23:28,856
I don’t know.

342
00:23:29,419 --> 00:23:30,154
Just give it to me.

343
00:23:42,477 --> 00:23:43,925
Want some wet food, baby?

344
00:23:47,215 --> 00:23:48,475
I’m not a cat.

345
00:23:48,475 --> 00:23:49,152
Nah.

346
00:23:51,208 --> 00:23:52,914
You’re my puppy.

347
00:23:55,663 --> 00:23:57,509
I’m not a dog. I’m human.

348
00:23:59,197 --> 00:24:00,132
Do this.

349
00:24:03,119 --> 00:24:03,993
Come on.

350
00:24:03,993 --> 00:24:04,880
Your other hand.

351
00:24:05,941 --> 00:24:06,961
Cheewa.

352
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:12,322
Now do this.

353
00:24:15,092 --> 00:24:16,796
Look, you’re just like a little puppy.

354
00:24:20,066 --> 00:24:21,683
This is silly.

355
00:24:23,090 --> 00:24:24,378
Talking back now, huh?

356
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:28,673
Please go back to sleep.

357
00:24:28,673 --> 00:24:29,657
This is so silly.

358
00:24:34,001 --> 00:24:35,440
Let me adjust your bed.

359
00:24:35,916 --> 00:24:36,969
Are you really going to let go of my hand?

360
00:24:38,419 --> 00:24:40,014
How would I adjust your bed otherwise?

361
00:24:48,139 --> 00:24:49,064
Lower it.

362
00:24:52,462 --> 00:24:54,354
You’re taking so long, Cheewa.

363
00:24:56,930 --> 00:24:58,484
Okay. That’s perfect.

364
00:24:58,874 --> 00:24:59,912
You’re so sweet.

365
00:25:00,626 --> 00:25:01,979
My puppy.

366
00:25:04,122 --> 00:25:04,917
Can you give me a massage?

367
00:25:04,917 --> 00:25:05,462
Massage my arm.

368
00:25:06,955 --> 00:25:08,218
You should go back to sleep.

369
00:25:09,495 --> 00:25:10,769
Give me a massage.

370
00:25:13,366 --> 00:25:14,186
Very good.

371
00:25:16,285 --> 00:25:17,265
I have a reward for you.

372
00:25:19,992 --> 00:25:21,553
I asked you to massage me,
not squeeze me.

373
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:23,623
Yes.

374
00:25:29,552 --> 00:25:31,412
Oh, don’t get up.

375
00:25:33,144 --> 00:25:34,524
Lie down and rest.

376
00:25:34,849 --> 00:25:36,322
I’ll sit down and keep you company.

377
00:25:36,322 --> 00:25:37,461
Oh, okay.

378
00:25:37,461 --> 00:25:38,232
Just a moment.

379
00:25:46,695 --> 00:25:47,707
How are you feeling?

380
00:25:48,941 --> 00:25:51,815
Um… I’m feeling much better now.

381
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:58,655
Does it still hurt anywhere?

382
00:25:59,910 --> 00:26:00,690
Um…

383
00:26:00,928 --> 00:26:02,962
Right now, just my legs.

384
00:26:03,633 --> 00:26:05,991
I guess I landed wrong.

385
00:26:06,489 --> 00:26:07,864
It just started hurting.

386
00:26:08,383 --> 00:26:10,544
Try to be careful next time.

387
00:26:10,804 --> 00:26:12,302
Your dad’s worried about you.

388
00:26:13,341 --> 00:26:15,270
So is your mom.

389
00:26:15,270 --> 00:26:19,863
Even though she doesn’t see you often,
she loves you and worries about you.

390
00:26:20,231 --> 00:26:23,689
She always talks about you.

391
00:26:26,178 --> 00:26:26,968
Uncle Rit.

392
00:26:26,968 --> 00:26:27,600
Yes?

393
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:33,858
After Mom marries you,

394
00:26:36,152 --> 00:26:37,788
will she still love me the same?

395
00:26:38,567 --> 00:26:39,329
Niran,

396
00:26:39,892 --> 00:26:41,093
listen to me.

397
00:26:41,656 --> 00:26:42,905
You know,

398
00:26:43,057 --> 00:26:45,966
when your dad called to tell her
you were in the hospital,

399
00:26:46,485 --> 00:26:48,733
she ran out of the house right away.

400
00:26:49,166 --> 00:26:51,219
She even put her shoes on the wrong feet.

401
00:26:53,189 --> 00:26:54,978
That made me realize that

402
00:26:55,151 --> 00:26:57,621
even if she marries me

403
00:26:58,443 --> 00:27:01,192
or any other man in the world,

404
00:27:01,950 --> 00:27:05,691
the man she loves the most
is you, Niran.

405
00:27:12,639 --> 00:27:14,831
Mom is happy these days, right?

406
00:27:15,026 --> 00:27:16,322
She’s doing okay, right?

407
00:27:19,525 --> 00:27:21,543
You have to take good care of her, Uncle Rit.

408
00:27:23,015 --> 00:27:23,798
Niran,

409
00:27:24,750 --> 00:27:27,758
I’ve actually been wanting to
talk to you about this for a while.

410
00:27:27,996 --> 00:27:29,175
You know,

411
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:32,670
your mom’s career is going well now.

412
00:27:32,886 --> 00:27:34,778
She always says

413
00:27:35,406 --> 00:27:37,396
she wants you to live with her.

414
00:27:40,859 --> 00:27:42,699
But don’t worry.

415
00:27:42,872 --> 00:27:44,627
Nothing will change.

416
00:27:44,865 --> 00:27:46,651
You can keep living your life as usual.

417
00:27:47,149 --> 00:27:48,322
You’ll go to the same school.

418
00:27:48,906 --> 00:27:51,100
You’ll just move in with us.

419
00:27:53,243 --> 00:27:57,034
And if you miss your dad,

420
00:27:57,294 --> 00:27:58,985
you can always visit him.

421
00:27:59,807 --> 00:28:05,306
I think that’ll be good for you
and your mom too.

422
00:28:05,306 --> 00:28:06,716
That way, she won’t have to worry.

423
00:28:08,015 --> 00:28:08,759
Alright?

424
00:28:10,469 --> 00:28:16,835
Please think about it.

425
00:28:26,130 --> 00:28:27,348
Are you okay, P’Niran?

426
00:28:28,127 --> 00:28:29,505
Yeah.

427
00:28:30,089 --> 00:28:31,533
It’s a little difficult, but I’m okay.

428
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:34,583
Then we can go celebrate now, right?

429
00:28:34,583 --> 00:28:35,231
Let’s go.

430
00:28:45,921 --> 00:28:47,034
Thank you so much, Da.

431
00:28:58,552 --> 00:29:01,953
You can always call me
about anything.

432
00:29:03,188 --> 00:29:03,971
You know that, right?

433
00:29:04,616 --> 00:29:05,475
I will, Mom.

434
00:29:09,622 --> 00:29:11,152
Get well soon, Niran.

435
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:13,667
Thank you.

436
00:29:23,305 --> 00:29:24,006
Thank you.

437
00:29:32,348 --> 00:29:33,407
Careful.

438
00:29:34,678 --> 00:29:35,586
Alright.

439
00:29:39,475 --> 00:29:40,953
You don't have to put your full weight on it.

440
00:29:41,100 --> 00:29:41,806
Can you manage?

441
00:29:42,138 --> 00:29:42,748
Yes.

442
00:29:42,748 --> 00:29:43,408
What should we do?

443
00:29:43,408 --> 00:29:44,729
Hold on to the table.

444
00:29:44,729 --> 00:29:45,256
Okay.

445
00:29:45,256 --> 00:29:45,756
Hold on to the table.

446
00:29:45,756 --> 00:29:46,786
Just a moment.

447
00:29:47,319 --> 00:29:48,030
Just a moment.

448
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:50,765
Alright.

449
00:29:51,877 --> 00:29:52,694
Come here.

450
00:29:52,694 --> 00:29:53,907
I’ll move this over here.

451
00:29:54,488 --> 00:29:55,161
Come on.

452
00:29:55,161 --> 00:29:55,894
Come over here.

453
00:30:02,916 --> 00:30:04,150
Alright.

454
00:30:04,596 --> 00:30:05,322
Are you hungry?

455
00:30:05,322 --> 00:30:05,904
Do you want to eat anything?

456
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:08,132
It’s okay. I just ate at the hospital.

457
00:30:08,132 --> 00:30:10,113
Oh, you’re right.

458
00:30:10,242 --> 00:30:13,012
Let me get you some fruit then.

459
00:30:13,012 --> 00:30:13,812
Here.

460
00:30:15,676 --> 00:30:16,664
Have some apples.

461
00:30:21,769 --> 00:30:22,516
Dad,

462
00:30:22,516 --> 00:30:24,569
when you did judo,

463
00:30:24,882 --> 00:30:26,258
did you always win awards?

464
00:30:26,350 --> 00:30:27,742
Oh.

465
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,975
Not to brag, but…

466
00:30:30,288 --> 00:30:31,971
Actually, yes.

467
00:30:31,971 --> 00:30:33,835
That’s because…

468
00:30:34,369 --> 00:30:36,058
I trained hard back then.

469
00:30:36,500 --> 00:30:39,188
I was really giving it my all.

470
00:30:39,888 --> 00:30:41,340
I was so into it.

471
00:30:44,584 --> 00:30:46,398
I went all out training.

472
00:30:46,767 --> 00:30:48,402
That’s why I got injured.

473
00:30:49,121 --> 00:30:51,463
I thought I’d recover
after resting for a little while.

474
00:30:53,619 --> 00:30:57,474
But after a month, I still hadn’t recovered.

475
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:00,550
Then a year went by.

476
00:31:01,858 --> 00:31:03,508
After a year,

477
00:31:05,111 --> 00:31:06,737
I started to accept that

478
00:31:06,921 --> 00:31:08,950
I might not be able to do judo again.

479
00:31:13,281 --> 00:31:14,026
Mm.

480
00:31:17,159 --> 00:31:18,493
Hey.

481
00:31:28,244 --> 00:31:29,199
Ah.

482
00:31:29,424 --> 00:31:30,467
Here it is.

483
00:31:35,056 --> 00:31:36,564
I won a lot of medals,

484
00:31:36,822 --> 00:31:41,788
but I love this one the most.

485
00:31:43,981 --> 00:31:48,542
Because I won it when I found out
I was going to have you.

486
00:31:53,592 --> 00:31:54,340
You can have it.

487
00:31:59,553 --> 00:32:00,530
Are you really giving it to me?

488
00:32:00,530 --> 00:32:01,148
Yeah.

489
00:32:17,952 --> 00:32:18,567
Hey.

490
00:32:20,516 --> 00:32:27,576
I know I’m not a very good dad.

491
00:32:30,316 --> 00:32:32,176
I’ve forced you to do things.

492
00:32:33,190 --> 00:32:34,630
I’ve made decisions for you.

493
00:32:38,039 --> 00:32:43,535
I’ve made you uncomfortable.

494
00:32:54,057 --> 00:32:55,172
I’m sorry.

495
00:33:03,183 --> 00:33:04,144
Um…

496
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:09,366
If you want to go live with your mom, I just…

497
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:18,079
I just want to ask you for one thing.

498
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:26,201
Come visit me sometimes.

499
00:33:27,417 --> 00:33:31,031
Come eat with me, you know?

500
00:33:34,843 --> 00:33:39,959
No matter who you choose to live with,

501
00:33:43,755 --> 00:33:45,244
I want you to know that

502
00:33:46,350 --> 00:33:47,660
I love you so much.

503
00:33:51,954 --> 00:33:53,719
More than anything in my life.

504
00:34:00,090 --> 00:34:00,590
Mm.

505
00:34:29,475 --> 00:34:31,159
It might be a little tough for you.

506
00:34:34,987 --> 00:34:36,633
You’ll have to keep putting up with me.

507
00:34:40,756 --> 00:34:42,074
How much did you overhear?

508
00:34:44,512 --> 00:34:49,788
I think that’ll be good for you
and for your mom too.

509
00:34:49,788 --> 00:34:51,240
That way, she won’t have to worry.

510
00:34:51,940 --> 00:34:58,132
Please think about it.

511
00:35:09,041 --> 00:35:10,676
Thank you so much, Uncle Rit,

512
00:35:11,155 --> 00:35:14,160
for being so kind to me
and doing so much for my mom.

513
00:35:14,879 --> 00:35:18,086
But I think Dad still needs me.

514
00:35:19,210 --> 00:35:20,493
And I still need him.

515
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:25,452
Even though my dad
isn’t as kind as other dads,

516
00:35:26,392 --> 00:35:28,985
he’s still the person I feel closest to.

517
00:35:30,916 --> 00:35:36,160
I still want to live with the guy
who’s always nagging and frowning,

518
00:35:37,413 --> 00:35:38,660
just like my dad.

519
00:35:44,871 --> 00:35:46,262
All I ask

520
00:35:49,572 --> 00:35:50,979
is that you understand me.

521
00:35:55,138 --> 00:35:57,873
I want you to be happy
with whatever I choose.

522
00:36:01,301 --> 00:36:02,412
Because no matter what,

523
00:36:05,969 --> 00:36:07,155
I’ll always choose you.

524
00:36:21,067 --> 00:36:21,817
Hey.

525
00:36:32,480 --> 00:36:33,595
Thank you.

526
00:36:36,009 --> 00:36:39,440
I’ll try to understand you better.

527
00:36:44,139 --> 00:36:44,723
I…

528
00:36:46,455 --> 00:36:49,267
I’ll be a good dad,

529
00:36:52,777 --> 00:36:54,196
just like other dads.

530
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:04,382
Free hug, Dad.

531
00:37:04,511 --> 00:37:06,071
Come on.

532
00:37:14,311 --> 00:37:15,467
Thank you, son.

533
00:37:16,156 --> 00:37:18,201
Thank you too, Dad.

534
00:37:19,970 --> 00:37:21,807
Thank you for being with me all this time.

535
00:37:24,055 --> 00:37:25,195
And always.

536
00:37:51,209 --> 00:37:52,370
Are you okay, P’Niran?

537
00:37:53,089 --> 00:37:54,439
Yeah.

538
00:37:55,047 --> 00:37:56,416
It’s a little difficult, but I’m okay.

539
00:37:58,627 --> 00:38:00,154
I’m asking about you and your dad.

540
00:38:00,523 --> 00:38:01,308
Ah.

541
00:38:01,824 --> 00:38:04,541
P’Niran has worked everything out,
Nong Cheewa.

542
00:38:04,781 --> 00:38:06,044
I feel so relieved.

543
00:38:07,876 --> 00:38:08,652
We love each other.

544
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:10,091
I even gave him a free hug.

545
00:38:10,496 --> 00:38:13,319
Then we can go celebrate now, right?

546
00:38:13,396 --> 00:38:14,111
Let’s go.

547
00:38:14,627 --> 00:38:16,518
Where does Nong Cheewa
want to take P’Niran today?

548
00:38:16,702 --> 00:38:18,005
P’Niran can go anywhere.

549
00:38:18,005 --> 00:38:19,858
But it might be a little difficult.

550
00:38:22,235 --> 00:38:23,279
It won’t.

551
00:38:24,827 --> 00:38:26,355
Hey, Niran!

552
00:38:26,355 --> 00:38:28,556
Niran!

553
00:38:28,556 --> 00:38:29,504
Hey!

554
00:38:32,084 --> 00:38:33,382
I thought it’d be just the two of us.

555
00:38:33,436 --> 00:38:35,283
Your friends have been
worried sick about you.

556
00:38:35,394 --> 00:38:36,497
Please let them join us.

557
00:38:38,156 --> 00:38:39,421
Hey, let me see.

558
00:38:39,421 --> 00:38:40,208
Does it hurt?

559
00:38:41,093 --> 00:38:41,982
Damn.

560
00:38:41,982 --> 00:38:42,853
That looks rough.

561
00:38:44,088 --> 00:38:45,923
It doesn’t hurt that much.

562
00:38:45,923 --> 00:38:47,266
It must be hard for you to walk.

563
00:38:47,377 --> 00:38:48,800
But I have a solution.

564
00:38:50,311 --> 00:38:51,243
I won’t go anywhere far.

565
00:38:51,243 --> 00:38:52,078
It’s hard for me to walk.

566
00:38:52,391 --> 00:38:54,159
Hey, what are you guys doing?

567
00:38:54,159 --> 00:38:56,686
- One, two, three.
- Hey!

568
00:38:56,778 --> 00:38:58,753
Now you’ll feel more comfortable.

569
00:38:58,753 --> 00:38:59,436
Let’s go hang out.

570
00:38:59,599 --> 00:39:00,417
Ouch!

571
00:39:00,509 --> 00:39:01,625
Hey, careful!

572
00:39:02,030 --> 00:39:02,694
Ready?

573
00:39:02,860 --> 00:39:03,481
Ready for what?

574
00:39:03,481 --> 00:39:04,242
Relax.

575
00:39:04,242 --> 00:39:04,848
Let me carry that, P’Thipok.

576
00:39:04,848 --> 00:39:05,749
Don’t tense up, buddy.

577
00:39:05,749 --> 00:39:06,493
No!

578
00:39:06,493 --> 00:39:07,073
Don’t tense up.

579
00:39:07,073 --> 00:39:08,871
- No! I’m scared!
- Don’t cry.

580
00:39:10,382 --> 00:39:11,162
Let’s go.

581
00:39:11,423 --> 00:39:12,360
One, two, three.

582
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:13,268
Go.

583
00:39:13,268 --> 00:39:14,783
Calm down, P’Niran.

584
00:39:14,783 --> 00:39:16,146
There’s nothing to be afraid of.

585
00:39:16,478 --> 00:39:18,214
Calm down.

586
00:39:19,756 --> 00:39:20,536
Hey, Yut.

587
00:39:20,676 --> 00:39:21,913
Are those two dating yet?

588
00:39:21,913 --> 00:39:22,878
No idea.

589
00:39:22,878 --> 00:39:23,867
Are you two dating—

590
00:39:23,867 --> 00:39:24,931
Don’t, P’Hem.

591
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:27,644
Thank you, guys,
for worrying about me.

592
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:29,431
You’re welcome.

593
00:39:39,899 --> 00:39:42,247
♪ But then you came ♪

594
00:39:42,247 --> 00:39:43,941
Damn! Can someone cover my ears?

595
00:39:43,941 --> 00:39:46,530
♪ And then tears ♪
Ugh!

596
00:39:46,530 --> 00:39:48,373
♪ You ♪

597
00:39:50,110 --> 00:39:51,888
Wait, where’s everyone?

598
00:39:51,888 --> 00:39:53,625
I don’t think your voice needs any music, man.

599
00:39:53,694 --> 00:39:54,710
Come back and listen to me!

600
00:39:56,665 --> 00:39:57,298
Damn!

601
00:39:57,422 --> 00:39:58,288
Where did they all go?

602
00:39:58,619 --> 00:39:59,831
Did you shoo them away?

603
00:40:00,230 --> 00:40:01,051
Yeah, it’s my fault.

604
00:40:01,478 --> 00:40:02,126
Just go.

605
00:40:02,828 --> 00:40:03,719
Don’t come here.

606
00:40:03,719 --> 00:40:04,410
Damn it.

607
00:40:04,589 --> 00:40:05,159
Thipok!

608
00:40:05,572 --> 00:40:06,577
Come and listen.

609
00:40:06,921 --> 00:40:07,720
Right, Cheewa?

610
00:40:08,023 --> 00:40:09,066
Tell them.

611
00:40:09,946 --> 00:40:11,220
Come and listen now.

612
00:40:11,895 --> 00:40:13,552
P’Niran has a great voice.

613
00:40:14,598 --> 00:40:15,171
See?

614
00:40:15,845 --> 00:40:17,143
Great voice?

615
00:40:17,143 --> 00:40:18,110
Let’s keep going.

616
00:40:18,110 --> 00:40:18,786
Come on.

617
00:40:19,969 --> 00:40:21,614
One, two, three.

618
00:40:21,614 --> 00:40:23,707
Hey, we ordered something delicious for you.

619
00:40:24,106 --> 00:40:25,068
Go ahead and eat first.

620
00:40:25,536 --> 00:40:26,269
I’ll go second.

621
00:40:27,260 --> 00:40:28,531
I’ll feed you.

622
00:40:28,531 --> 00:40:29,435
Hey.

623
00:40:29,435 --> 00:40:30,884
Aren’t you guys spoiling me too much?

624
00:40:30,884 --> 00:40:31,956
I just hurt my legs.

625
00:40:31,956 --> 00:40:32,779
I’m fine.

626
00:40:33,192 --> 00:40:35,293
Come on. When you passed out that day,

627
00:40:35,293 --> 00:40:37,069
we were scared out of our minds.

628
00:40:37,069 --> 00:40:38,939
We didn’t think
you’d push yourself that much.

629
00:40:38,939 --> 00:40:41,312
Next time you’re stressed,
tell your friends.

630
00:40:41,477 --> 00:40:42,649
Yeah, yeah.

631
00:40:42,842 --> 00:40:44,975
I’m sorry I let myself get like this.

632
00:40:44,975 --> 00:40:46,964
Life is just like stellar evolution.

633
00:40:46,964 --> 00:40:48,153
Stars are born,

634
00:40:48,359 --> 00:40:50,545
shine bright, expand,

635
00:40:50,545 --> 00:40:52,282
then explode and become new stars.

636
00:40:52,337 --> 00:40:54,775
Our lives have calm and
chaotic moments too. It’s no different.

637
00:40:55,050 --> 00:40:58,584
Damn.

638
00:40:59,368 --> 00:41:01,116
That’s so deep, Jomyut.

639
00:41:05,933 --> 00:41:07,078
Thank you, guys,

640
00:41:07,877 --> 00:41:08,716
for worrying about me.

641
00:41:09,032 --> 00:41:10,035
You’re welcome.

642
00:41:13,432 --> 00:41:14,707
Are we still needed here?

643
00:41:15,780 --> 00:41:16,592
Of course.

644
00:41:16,922 --> 00:41:20,127
We’re the air they breathe
when they flirt with each other.

645
00:41:31,185 --> 00:41:32,181
We’re almost at my house.

646
00:41:32,181 --> 00:41:33,836
I can walk from here.

647
00:41:33,836 --> 00:41:35,078
How are you going to get there?

648
00:41:35,078 --> 00:41:35,841
Limping?

649
00:41:36,336 --> 00:41:37,879
I’ll take P’Niran home.

650
00:41:38,030 --> 00:41:39,744
We’re going the same way anyway.

651
00:41:42,909 --> 00:41:45,074
Put the backpack on your back.

652
00:41:45,569 --> 00:41:46,161
Why?

653
00:41:51,074 --> 00:41:51,723
And?

654
00:41:51,833 --> 00:41:52,832
Hop on my back.

655
00:41:53,149 --> 00:41:53,649
Huh?

656
00:41:54,805 --> 00:41:55,528
Okay.

657
00:41:55,611 --> 00:41:56,664
Are you sure I’ll be fine?

658
00:41:57,118 --> 00:42:00,096
Whoa!

659
00:42:02,958 --> 00:42:03,882
Get home safe.

660
00:42:04,295 --> 00:42:04,946
Hey, Yut.

661
00:42:05,455 --> 00:42:06,802
Are those two dating yet?

662
00:42:07,449 --> 00:42:08,397
No idea.

663
00:42:08,961 --> 00:42:10,690
Can you ask them? I want to know too.

664
00:42:11,117 --> 00:42:11,617
Oh?

665
00:42:11,961 --> 00:42:13,825
Does your universe not know about it?

666
00:42:14,265 --> 00:42:14,765
Not at all.

667
00:42:14,765 --> 00:42:15,265
No.

668
00:42:15,673 --> 00:42:16,236
Ugh!

669
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:17,185
I’ll ask!

670
00:42:17,295 --> 00:42:18,548
No need to wait for the stars.

671
00:42:19,112 --> 00:42:20,935
Hey, Niran, are you two—

672
00:42:24,376 --> 00:42:25,751
I want to know!

673
00:42:27,223 --> 00:42:29,053
Don’t you guys want to know?

674
00:42:29,397 --> 00:42:30,444
Are you two dating—

675
00:42:30,444 --> 00:42:31,352
Don’t, P’Hem.

676
00:42:33,045 --> 00:42:34,085
Stop talking.

677
00:42:35,021 --> 00:42:35,752
Never mind.

678
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:37,065
Just go home.

679
00:42:37,203 --> 00:42:38,476
If you’re tired, take a break.

680
00:42:49,506 --> 00:42:50,433
Why are you laughing?

681
00:42:51,782 --> 00:42:53,736
Why didn’t you answer
your friends’ question?

682
00:42:54,218 --> 00:42:55,418
Why would I answer other people?

683
00:42:55,556 --> 00:42:56,966
I’ll only answer when you ask.

684
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:02,579
I have a question.

685
00:43:03,762 --> 00:43:04,380
What is it?

686
00:43:09,821 --> 00:43:11,349
Can we be a couple now?

687
00:43:17,783 --> 00:43:18,633
Turn your face toward me.

688
00:43:25,031 --> 00:43:26,393
I’m not going to answer directly.

689
00:44:10,546 --> 00:44:12,666
P’Cheewin is picking us up a bit late this evening.

690
00:44:12,749 --> 00:44:14,641
I need to prepare for the tri-school game.

691
00:44:14,641 --> 00:44:16,453
It’s okay. Just do your work. I can wait.

692
00:44:16,453 --> 00:44:17,435
It’s today.

693
00:44:17,435 --> 00:44:18,789
The basketball game looks so good.

694
00:44:18,789 --> 00:44:19,643
Glasses is here.

695
00:44:19,877 --> 00:44:20,962
You’re playing basketball?

696
00:44:21,168 --> 00:44:21,825
Am I cool?

697
00:44:22,059 --> 00:44:24,176
But now you’re cool in other people’s eyes too.

698
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:25,630
Can I be your boyfriend now?

699
00:44:27,089 --> 00:44:29,305
Will your dad really be okay with this?

700
00:44:29,305 --> 00:44:31,247
Of course. I just don’t really invite anyone over.

701
00:44:31,343 --> 00:44:33,709
You want me to listen to music at your house as what, exactly?
